<div class="summation">
  <h3>Translator's Summary</h3>
  <p>
    Reb Noson unifies the entire Pesach–Omer–Shavuos calendar under one master-key drawn
    from <em>Likutay Moharan</em> 1:31: <strong>holy longing</strong>
    (<span style="font-style:italic;color:#f5c842">kisufin d'kedushah</span>). Every
    halacha discussed — the prohibition of blood, salting, rinsing, the mikveh — becomes
    a face of this single spiritual reality.
  </p>
  <div class="flow">
    <span class="flow-item">Shemiras ha-Bris</span>
    <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>
    <span class="flow-item">Kisufin d'Kedushah</span>
    <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>
    <span class="flow-item">Nefashos / Nekudos made</span>
    <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>
    <span class="flow-item">Torah letters formed</span>
    <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>
    <span class="flow-item">Torah received on Shavuos</span>
  </div>
  <p style="margin-top:1em">
    <strong>The blood/water transformation</strong> runs through every section:
    blood (= animal soul, din) → kisufin d'kedushah (= chesed) → milk / water (= Torah).
    Salt draws out evil blood; water (Torah) completes the purification.
    Lag Ba'Omer / Rabbi Shimon bar Yochai is the culminating revelation: rolling
    the stone from the well, releasing the hidden waters of Torah —
    <em>maimei ha-chesed</em> — made possible only through the covenant of love.
  </p>
